From cb8d762cdfc7628713a3e1df2044f7d5852ebddd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Donach's Bot <bot@braiins.cz>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 19:09:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: wide n==1 ternary/binary mul_mat_vec path + GCN
 tuning knobs

- TERNARY_WIDE: dedicated n==1 matvec for Q1_0/Q2_0, 32 weights/thread/iter
  via packed16 loads, activations staged in registers across rows.
- TERNARY_F16 (GGML_VK_TERNARY_F16=1): fp16 staging + packed f16
  accumulation (v_pk_fma_f16) in the wide path; halves staged VGPRs and fma
  count. Block-scale correction stays fp32.
- PACKED_K (GGML_VK_MM_PACKED=1): mul_mm f16acc variants for Q1_0/Q2_0
  accumulate even/odd k in the two lanes of one f16vec2 per output -> one
  v_pk_fma_f16 per k-pair instead of two scalar v_fma_f16 (GCN runs scalar
  f16 fma at fp32 rate).
- GGML_VK_TERNARY_ROWS: rows/workgroup knob for the wide path (1..16).
- GGML_VK_GCN_SUBGROUP_REDUCE=1: opt GCN into subgroup reductions.
- GGML_VK_TILE_{L,M,S}: runtime warptile override (11 csv uints) for the
  dequant mmq pipelines, wg_denoms follow BM/BN.
